// The C ABI exports of std/crypto (decisions 0204, 0207): like cabi.xo,
// every top level function here is called by the C runtime as
// xo_x_<name>; std/llrt/xo_crypto.c's Ed25519 (C until it is constant
// time Xo, the zero-C audit's B09) calls them, so std/native/crypto.xo
// imports this module. A program without std/crypto takes the C's weak
// definitions, which fault (gotchas/exports-grow-every-program.md).
use native/llrt/digest

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SHA-512 (xo_crypto.c's Ed25519)

/// SHA-512 of the an bytes at a, then the bn at b, then the cn at c (any
/// of them 0 with a null address), into the 64 bytes at out.
fn sha512_3(a: Int, an: Int, b: Int, bn: Int, c: Int, cn: Int, out: Int) { digest.sha512_3(a, an, b, bn, c, cn, out) }
